  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "At Yu Tian heroes assembly in Northern Plains, a loud voice answers Liu Wen Wu’s need for a fighter, and the crowd parts for a tall, heavy-built man with ink-dark skin, a fierce mouth and wide nose, and snowy white hair and beard like a lion’s mane. Someone names him an inkman, and narration states rockman, eggman, hairy man, and inkman are variant men, not Ren Zu’s descendants, with inkman homeland on Book Mountain. He bows to Liu Wen Wu as big brother, and Liu Wen Wu introduces him as Mo Shi Kuang, whom he swore brotherhood to in earlier years.",
      "chapters": [
        497
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_yu_tian",
        "reg_northern_plains",
        "char_liu_wen_wu",
        "char_ren_zu",
        "loc_book_mountain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He jumps onto the stage when Viper Prince beckons him, claps his palms, and an invisible qi path force crushes Viper Prince into minced meat. Onlookers gasp at rank four peak stage qi path in that one move.",
      "chapters": [
        497
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_viper_prince"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The next chapter states he is a rank four peak stage expert who cultivates qi path, and that he is a rare successful variant man cultivator. He is also extremely addicted to fighting, unlike ordinary inkmen. He next stamps Hei Lou Lan’s defensive commander Hei Xiu Yi nearly to death with a huge qi foot, then sweeps a qi arm outside the stage until the heroes assembly collapses into a chaotic battle.",
      "chapters": [
        498
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_hei_lou_lan",
        "char_hei_xiu_yi"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When Fang Yuan’s wolf army arrives, Mo Shi Kuang stands beside Liu Wen Wu as a nine feet tall ink man with black body and white hair, named the number one fierce general in that Imperial Court competition. Liu Wen Wu calls him third brother, and Mo Shi Kuang offers to attack and kill Chang Shan Yin directly, then reminds him of second brother still in closed cultivation.",
      "chapters": [
        499
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "loc_imperial_court",
        "char_chang_shan_yin"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A later stretch names that second brother Ouyang Bi Sang, a demonic transformation path Gu Master who met Liu Wen Wu and Mo Shi Kuang at an inheritance site and swore brotherhood with them.",
      "chapters": [
        525
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_ouyang_bi_sang",
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He is tall with a beefed up body, a fierce mouth and wide nose, skin as dark as ink, with snowy white lush hair and beard that blend together like a lion’s mane. White hair and black skin make an unusual appearance.",
      "chapters": [
        497
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "His snow-white hair sways loosely in the air, and his beard flutters.",
      "chapters": [
        498
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "He is a nine feet tall ink man, his body black with white hair, standing like a guardian.",
      "chapters": [
        499
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cunning Gentleman Sun Shi Han lists Mo Shi Kuang and Ouyang Bi Sang as rank four peak stage experts with battle strength of rank five among Liu tribe’s fierce offense.",
      "chapters": [
        527
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "battle-strength-of-rank-five",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_sun_shi_han",
        "fac_liu_tribe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Against Zhu Zai he fights as a qi path Gu Master using qi armor and qi explosion Gu rather than true strength path, later kills Zhu Zai with the incomplete killer move World Devouring Qi, and vomits blood from the backlash while laughing.",
      "chapters": [
        531
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "battle-strength-of-rank-five",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_zhu_zai",
        "move_world_devouring_qi"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "With Liu Wen Wu and Ouyang Bi Sang he forms the three brothers’ killer move Three Head Six Arms, a twenty foot three-headed six-armed monster whose heads match the three of them.",
      "chapters": [
        534
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "battle-strength-of-rank-five",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "move_three_head_six_arms"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Tai Bai Yun Sheng later recalls that among the few qi path cultivators he has seen in northern plains, the strongest and most recent was Liu Wen Wu’s sworn brother, the variant human Mo Shi Kuang.",
      "chapters": [
        584
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "battle-strength-of-rank-five",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_tai_bai_yun_sheng"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "His white hair flutters, his black skin and panther-like eyes shine. A crazed look appears on his coal-like inky black skin.",
      "chapters": [
        531
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "contest-battlefield",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
